#wap to check if a list contains a palindrome of elements or not.

##palindrome refers to the term,when we read a tuple from starting to end  and  end to starting the order of tuple is same. example- 121 if we read this from starting and end it will follow same order .

list = [1, 2, 3, 2, 1, 4]
# list2 = [1, 2, 2, 1]

copy_list = list.copy()
copy_list.reverse()


if(copy_list == list):
    print("The list is a palindrome")
else:
    print("The list is not a palindrome")







